---
// Reader: a programme team or implementer assessing the authoring workspace.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import Film from '../../components/Film.astro';
import { askQuestionHref } from '../../data/contact';
---
<Base title="Registry Studio | Registry Stack" description="Review and configure registries and services with your technical team. Registry Studio is an authoring workspace available as a Preview.">
  <SiteHeader current="studio" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="studio-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Registry Studio · Preview</p>
      <h1 id="studio-title">Review and configure registries and services together.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">An authoring workspace for programme teams and implementers. Understand the records and service steps, review proposed changes and prepare a version for your technical team to run.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href={askQuestionHref('Registry Studio')}>Ask about Studio</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#workspace">Explore the workspace</a></div>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="workspace" aria-labelledby="model-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="model-title">See the service your team is defining.</h2><p>Review the record model, the changes people may request and the steps used to handle a service. Keep programme and technical discussions connected to the same definitions.</p></div>
      <div class="value-grid"><article><h3>Records</h3><p>Inspect the information the register keeps and review changes to its structure.</p></article><article><h3>Permitted changes</h3><p>See the actions that can change a record and the rules your team must confirm.</p></article><article><h3>Service steps</h3><p>Follow the service map and review how the work is organized.</p></article></div>
      <Film
        name="registry-stack-studio-film"
        title="Registry Stack Studio: build a service from the same parts"
        caption="A fictional city council builds a market stall permit service in Studio. An approver signs before handover, and a later change goes through the same checks and approval."
      />
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="fit" aria-labelledby="review-title"><div class="section-inner approach-split">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="review-title">Review a change before handing it over.</h2><p>Check proposed edits against the product’s checks and save a version. Prepare the product files and handover information for the team responsible for running the service.</p><p>Studio authors the configuration. Your operating team remains responsible for deploying and operating the service.</p></div>
      <div class="editorial-callout"><h3>Start a draft from existing documents</h3><p>Studio includes AI-assisted drafting. Use source documents to prepare a draft brief, review the questions and findings, and confirm what the service should do.</p><p>The draft is a starting point for review, not an approved service definition.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/ai/service-design/">See the service design approach <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="access-title"><div class="section-inner"><h2 id="access-title">Discuss Studio with Aubex.</h2><p>Studio is available as a Preview. Contact Aubex about access. It is a commercial authoring tool with separate licensing terms; the core runtime software’s Apache-2.0 licence does not cover Studio. You do not need Studio to run or change a service: it writes the same configuration files your team can review and edit without it.</p><div class="section-links"><a class="button button-primary" href={askQuestionHref('Registry Studio')}>Ask about Studio</a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/customization/">Explore implementation support</a></div></div></section>
  </main><SiteFooter />
</Base>
